{"text":"     1\t// Package blogger provides a client for the Blogger API v3.\n     2\tpackage blogger\n     3\t\n     4\timport (\n     5\t\t\"context\"\n     6\t\t\"net/http\"\n     7\t\n     8\t\t\"google.golang.org/api/blogger/v3\"\n     9\t\t\"google.golang.org/api/option\"\n    10\t)\n    11\t\n    12\tconst defaultBaseServiceURL = \"https://blogger.googleapis.com/\"\n    13\t\n    14\t// Client is a thin wrapper over the generated Blogger v3 service, exposing one\n    15\t// accessor per API resource.\n    16\ttype Client struct {\n    17\t\t// Service is the underlying generated Blogger v3 service.\n    18\t\tService *blogger.Service\n    19\t\n    20\t\tctx context.Context\n    21\t\n    22\t\thttpClient *http.Client\n    23\t\n    24\t\tbaseServiceURL string\n    25\t}\n    26\t\n    27\t// NewClient creates a Client using the supplied client options. When no HTTP\n    28\t// client is supplied through opts, google.golang.org/api builds one from the\n    29\t// default application credentials.\n    30\tfunc NewClient(ctx context.Context, opts ...option.ClientOption) (*Client, error) {\n    31\t\tsvc, err := blogger.NewService(ctx, opts...)\n    32\t\tif err != nil {\n    33\t\t\treturn nil, err\n    34\t\t}\n    35\t\n    36\t\treturn &Client{\n    37\t\t\tService:        svc,\n    38\t\t\tctx:            ctx,\n    39\t\t\tbaseServiceURL: svc.BasePath,\n    40\t\t}, nil\n    41\t}\n    42\t\n    43\t// NewRawClient creates a Client backed by a caller-provided http.Client. It\n    44\t// never fails and requires no credentials; use it when you manage\n    45\t// authentication and transport yourself. The supplied client must not be nil.\n    46\tfunc NewRawClient(httpClient *http.Client) *Client {\n    47\t\treturn &Client{\n    48\t\t\tctx:            context.Background(),\n    49\t\t\thttpClient:     httpClient,\n    50\t\t\tbaseServiceURL: defaultBaseServiceURL,\n    51\t\t}\n    52\t}\n    53\t\n    54\t// WithContext returns a copy of the Client bound to ctx. The underlying Service\n    55\t// and http.Client are shared, so nothing else about the Client changes.\n    56\tfunc (c *Client) WithContext(ctx context.Context) *Client {\n    57\t\tclone := *c\n    58\t\tclone.ctx = ctx\n    59\t\treturn &clone\n    60\t}\n    61\t\n    62\t// HTTPClient returns the transport the Client sends through, or nil when the\n    63\t// Client was built from the default credentials.\n    64\tfunc (c *Client) HTTPClient() *http.Client {\n    65\t\treturn c.httpClient\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\t// Blogs returns a builder for the blogs resource.\n    69\tfunc (c *Client) Blogs() *blogger.BlogsService {\n    70\t\treturn blogger.NewBlogsService(c.Service)\n    71\t}\n    72\t\n    73\t// Comments returns a builder for the comments resource.\n    74\tfunc (c *Client) Comments() *blogger.CommentsService {\n    75\t\treturn blogger.NewCommentsService(c.Service)\n    76\t}\n    77\t\n    78\t// Pages returns a builder for the pages resource.\n    79\tfunc (c *Client) Pages() *blogger.PagesService {\n    80\t\treturn blogger.NewPagesService(c.Service)\n    81\t}\n    82\t\n    83\t// Posts returns a builder for the posts resource.\n    84\tfunc (c *Client) Posts() *blogger.PostsService {\n    85\t\treturn blogger.NewPostsService(c.Service)\n    86\t}\n    87\t\n    88\t// Users returns a builder for the users resource.\n    89\tfunc (c *Client) Users() *blogger.UsersService {\n    90\t\treturn blogger.NewUsersService(c.Service)\n    91\t}\n    92\t\n    93\t// BlogUserInfos returns a builder for the blogUserInfos resource.\n    94\tfunc (c *Client) BlogUserInfos() *blogger.BlogUserInfosService {\n    95\t\treturn blogger.NewBlogUserInfosService(c.Service)\n    96\t}\n    97\t\n    98\t// PageViews returns a builder for the pageViews resource.\n    99\tfunc (c *Client) PageViews() *blogger.PageViewsService {\n   100\t\treturn blogger.NewPageViewsService(c.Service)\n   101\t}\n   102\t\n   103\t// PostUserInfos returns a builder for the postUserInfos resource.\n   104\tfunc (c *Client) PostUserInfos() *blogger.PostUserInfosService {\n   105\t\treturn blogger.NewPostUserInfosService(c.Service)\n   106\t}\n=== README\n# blogger-go\n\nA Go SDK for the [Blogger API v3](https://developers.google.com/blogger/docs/3.0/getting_started),\ngenerated from Google's discovery document and layered over the official\n[`google.golang.org/api/blogger/v3`](https://pkg.go.dev/google.golang.org/api/blogger/v3) client.\n\nThe module provides:\n\n- `Client` - the entry point for talking to Blogger, wrapping OAuth2 credentials\n  and the upstream generated service.\n- `gen/schemas` - model structs derived from the discovery document.\n- `gen/services` - one implementation file per API resource (posts, blogs, comments, ...).\n- `gen/builder` - request builder types used by the generated service files.\n- `internal` - shared helpers that are not part of the public API.\n\n> Status: skeleton. Service methods and model structs land in later iterations;\n> the layout and public entry points are stable.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\ngo get github.com/itokun99/blogger-go\n```\n\n## Minimal example\n\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log\"\n\n\tblogger \"github.com/itokun99/blogger-go\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\tctx := context.Background()\n\n\t// auth.TokenSourceFromJSON builds an OAuth2 token source from a\n\t// downloaded \"credentials.json\" and a cached token file.\n\tts, err := blogger.TokenSourceFromJSON(\"credentials.json\", \"token.json\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tlog.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\n\tclient, err := blogger.NewClient(ctx, ts)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tlog.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\n\tblog, err := client.Blogger.Blogs.Get(\"1234567890\").Do()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tlog.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tfmt.Println(blog.Name)\n}\n```","details":{"status":"completed"},"images":[],"hasError":false}
